# std/remove — one of the file tools (std/files holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Remove a file, a directory with everything under it, or a whole source tree. `root` is what to remove, such as sources/repo/00-base-2. A directory left empty goes too. Prefer this over rm via bash.
@writer
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/files
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=remove --help=$HELP
